#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:180
#: 97ca26132b804b7b97c404a03a568f9c
msgid "Loading Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:182
#: 30c7f1eb7ec94cc198ef2894d10b0d69
msgid "The RADIX 2 HD uses a proprietary bootloader which needs a firmware file in a custom file format. There are several ways of obtaining the firmware file, as explained below. Once you have obtained the file, copy it to the USB drive that appears when connecting the RADIX 2 HD to your computer when it is in bootloader mode (hold the BOOT button and release when connecting to USB). Once it finishes copying, safely remove the drive. At this point the RADIX 2 HD will reboot and run the ArduPilot firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:184
#: 26ff3d8d5d4c4a0f8ec1f76a5fcc3b5d
msgid "When using ArduPilot, it is necessary to have a microSD card inserted, without it the firmware won't run."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:187
#: 4ef1cc13fa9a48ca98a12208a7279f77
msgid "Option 1: Download the Firmware File the BrainFPV Website"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:189
#: 9462c1fbb2ac4515a32f1687bd8cb749
msgid "The easiest way to get firmware files for your RADIX 2 HD is to download them from the BrainFPV website. You can do so `here <https://www.brainfpv.com/firmware/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:192
#: 9fd487ac81d14925ae081b49256cb9f9
msgid "Option 2: Download the Firmware From the ArduPilot Firmware Server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:194
#: c6b05c93322643db9321f58550e3abe6
msgid "Download the ELF file from the `ArduPilot Firmware Server <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__. Make sure you download the file for the \"RADIX2HD\" target. For example, the ELF file for ArduCopter is called \"arducopter.elf\". At this time, only the 4.5 (\"latest\") versions are available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:196
#: 9937edfd242b45ce9d1c706c9c850cb5
msgid "In order to use the ELF file with your RADIX 2 HD, it needs to be converted using the BrainFPV Firmware Packer. This utility is implemented in Python, so you will need a Python installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:198
#: c59655c3c4354006b931aa15734174d3
msgid "If you are using Linux, use your package manager to install Python 3. If you are using Windows, download the Python 3 installer from the Python Website and run it. When installing, make sure to select \"Add Python to PATH\", so you will be able to use Python from the Windows Command Prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:200
#: 79646f0ab36a40cea4922315afa54b9f
msgid "After installing Python, start the Command Prompt and install the BrainFPV Firmware Packer using the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:207
#: bb2ef19bea4a4905bddb7a4855213972
msgid "After installing it, you can use the following command to convert the \"arducopter.elf\" (or other vehicle elf file) file to a \"arducopter.bin\" file that can be used with the RADIX 2 HD:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:215
#: 165152f2da504f3e93b26a1bf1009e12
msgid "Option 3: Compile the Firmware Yourself"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:217
#: 49f81d86d33e4ebd8da2ce877592e86c
msgid "If you have a working :ref:`ArduPilot build environment<building-the-code>`, you can compile the firmware yourself and then convert it to the format needed by the BrainFPV bootloader. You will also need the BrainFPV Firmware Packer to do so. Install it using the \"pip install\" command shown above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:219
#: 344fc4db9232424494bb9fba2282d8f7
msgid "For Copter, build the firmware as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-radix2hd.rst:226
#: 65356c3c49864d8e9e022589fa63e30e
msgid "other vehicles can be built, but the RADIX2HD is targeted primarily for copter applications. Then use the firmware packer script to create the firmware file that can be used with the BrainFPV bootloader:"
msgstr ""

